  <section class="content-block">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="text-center section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-section">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How much space do I need for a pickleball court?</h3>
          <p>While the playing area is 20' × 44', we recommend a minimum total area of 30' × 60' to allow adequate out-of-bounds space. For optimal play, 34' × 64' provides comfortable clearance areas around the court.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can I convert my tennis court to pickleball?</h3>
          <p>Absolutely! Tennis courts can accommodate multiple pickleball courts. One tennis court can fit four pickleball courts. We can add pickleball lines while maintaining the tennis lines, or completely resurface for dedicated pickleball use.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What's the typical construction timeline?</h3>
          <p>Most residential pickleball courts are completed in 5-7 business days after base preparation. This includes excavation, base installation, surface application, line marking, and net installation. Weather and site conditions may affect timing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Do you handle permits and HOA approvals?</h3>
          <p>Yes, we assist with the permit process and provide professional drawings and specifications needed for HOA or city approval. Our experience with local regulations helps ensure smooth approval processes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What maintenance is required for pickleball courts?</h3>
          <p>Pickleball courts require minimal maintenance. Regular cleaning, annual inspection for cracks, and periodic line refreshing (every 3-5 years) will keep your court in excellent condition. We offer maintenance programs for hassle-free upkeep.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

